[[SECTION]]
UID: MEMBERS-OBJECTIVES
TITLE: Member's Functions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-20
TITLE: Member Accounts
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should let members manage their own accounts and let authorized administrators manage member accounts.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members should be able to update their own membership information without first contacting the organization. Administrators need to correct and maintain those accounts for the organization.
<<<
OWNER: Customer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-18
TITLE: Member Elections
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should support elections by the membership for GSSC leadership.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
GSSC elections should be digitized and accessible.
<<<
OWNER: Customer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-19
TITLE: Member Publications
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should support publications by the membership.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
GSSC publications should be streamlined without requiring developer intervention.
<<<
OWNER: Customer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-21
TITLE: Member Directory
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should give members a directory of fellow members and the contact information those members make available for collaboration within the organization.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members need one another's contact information in order to collaborate. The directory is for members.
<<<
OWNER: Customer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: DEVELOPMENT-OBJECTIVES
TITLE: Development Objectives

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-1
TITLE: Public-Facing Domain
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should have a public-facing primary domain.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Guests, visitors, and interested persons should be able to learn more about the GSSC.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-2
TITLE: Member Subdomain
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should have a members-only subdomain.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Members of the GSSC should have an internal area where they can manage their memberships, access members-only resources, and perform private actions related to the GSSC.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-3
TITLE: Unified Backend
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should have a unified backend supporting the public and members-only spaces.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This will enable changes to the public site to be made from the members-only area by members with sufficient permissions. It will allow for content to be shared between the two spaces without duplication.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-4
TITLE: Website Security
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should protect visitor and member information, and the integrity of published content, against unauthorized access, modification, and disclosure.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An insecure site puts the people who use it, and the society's records, at risk.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-5
TITLE: Maintainer Usability
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should be modifiable by individuals without programming knowledge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This will reduce load on the developers by empowering maintainers to make changes they desire at will.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-6
TITLE: Multiuser Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should allow more than one authorized person to modify content at the same time, without blocking one another or losing each other's changes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Several officers and volunteers need to update the site during the same period, and that work should stay off the developers.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-OBJ-7
TITLE: Member-Driven Content
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website should let authorized users create and publish content, including publications, newsletters, and events, without developer intervention.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Pages which could be generated by users, such as new publications, newsletters, events, etc. should not require developer intervention.
<<<
OWNER: Developer
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-1
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]
